import "core"
import obsidian("artifacts/catln-tasks")
import obsidian("artifacts/catln-tasks/Tasks.md")


# Tests importing an Obsidian vault which runs the Tasks community plugin. Every checkbox of such a
  vault is read as a /Data/Note/Task/Obsidian, holding the line as it was written and the plugin's
  own writing read out of it, where a checkbox of the vault beside this one — artifacts/catln-test,
  which runs no plugin — is read as a /Data/Note/Task/Simple.
  The note is named as well as the vault, for the reason obsidian.ct names its notes: a vault does
  not import the notes it holds, so a golden test walking out from here would reach the vault and
  stop.
  A vault can only be set one way, so what a vault set some other way reads as — a global filter,
  the dataview notation, a status the vault named itself — is covered by ObsidianTaskTests rather
  than by a fixture for each.
main{io -> IO}= io.exit(val= 0)
